---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Image from '../../components/OptimizedImage.astro';
import nearMeImg from '../../../assets/Near-Me-Local-Search.png';

const blogPostingSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BlogPosting",
  "headline": "How to Choose a Web Designer in Cleveland County",
  "description": "How to choose a web designer in Cleveland County — the questions to ask, the red flags to avoid, and what a site that actually generates leads looks like.",
  "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Dave Richardson", "jobTitle": "Founder / Lead Developer", "url": "https://www.shelbywebco.com/about/" },
  "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Shelby Web Company", "logo": { "@type": "ImageObject", "url": "https://www.shelbywebco.com/og-image.jpg" } },
  "mainEntityOfPage": "https://www.shelbywebco.com/blog/best-web-designers-near-me/",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-15",
  "dateModified": "2026-10-22"
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How to Choose a Web Designer in Cleveland County"
  description="How to choose a web designer in Cleveland County — the questions to ask, the red flags to avoid, and what a site that actually generates leads looks like."
>
  <script is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(blogPostingSchema)} type="application/ld+json"></script>

  <article class="pt-24 pb-16 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <header class="mb-10 text-center">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 mb-6 px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full border border-brand-blue/20 bg-brand-blue/5">
          <span class="text-brand-cyan text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">Shelby Web Official</span>
          <span class="w-1 h-1 rounded-full bg-brand-sky/30"></span>
          <span class="text-white/90 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest">August 2026</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="font-heading text-5xl md:text-7xl font-black text-white mb-8 tracking-tight leading-[1.1]">
          How to Choose a Web Designer in <br />
          <span class="text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-cyan to-brand-blue">Cleveland County</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-white/90 text-sm uppercase tracking-widest">By Dave Richardson — Founder / Lead Developer, Shelby Web Company</p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose prose-invert prose-lg max-w-none">
        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          If you typed "web designers near me" into Google, you got a results page full of directory listings, review widgets, and agencies all claiming to be the best. That is not much help when you are the one hiring and living with the result.
        </p>
        <p class="text-white mb-12 leading-relaxed">
          The short version: ask who will be working on the site, ask what happens after launch, and ask to see a real local example. Those three questions eliminate most of the field. Here is the full checklist, written for Cleveland County and Gaston County business owners choosing between <a href="/web-design-shelby-nc/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">web designers in Shelby</a>, <a href="/web-design-gastonia-nc/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">Gastonia</a>, and <a href="/web-design-kings-mountain-nc/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">Kings Mountain</a>.
        </p>

        <div class="my-12 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl max-w-[640px] mx-auto">
          <Image src={nearMeImg} alt="Local 'near me' web design search results" class="w-full h-auto" />
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8">"Near Me" Should Actually Mean Something</h2>
        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          A lot of agencies that show up for local searches aren't local at all — they're national outfits running location-targeted ads, or freelancers halfway across the country who bought a local phone number. That's not automatically bad, but it does change what you're getting.
        </p>
        <p class="text-white mb-4 leading-relaxed">A genuinely local web designer:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-white mb-12 leading-relaxed">
          <li>Understands your specific market — who's searching for you, and where they're coming from (a designer who knows <a href="/web-design-gastonia-nc/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">Gastonia</a> isn't just guessing at your audience)</li>
          <li>Can meet in person if something needs to be worked through face-to-face</li>
          <li>Has a reputation in the actual community, not just a five-star badge that could belong to anyone</li>
          <li>Is invested in your success because your success is their local reputation</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          At Shelby Web Company we're literally just a phone call away. We are an actual human voice. And we are here 24/7.
        </p>
        <p class="text-white mb-12 leading-relaxed">
          If a "near me" result turns out to be a call center for a big out-of-state agency, that's worth knowing before you commit.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8">The 5-Question Interview Checklist</h2>
        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          Before you sign anything, ask these five questions. Good local designers answer them without hesitating, because they aren't worried about you leaving.
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-4 mb-16">
          {[
            "Do you build with performance (LCP/FID) or just templates?",
            "How specifically will you optimize for local 'Map Pack' search?",
            "Is the branding research included or do I provide everything?",
            "Who do I call at 6:30 PM on a Tuesday if the site has an issue?",
            "What is the actual data-driven path from a visitor to a phone call?"
          ].map((q, i) => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4 p-4 bg-brand-dark/30 rounded-xl border border-white/5">
              <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-brand-cyan/20 text-brand-cyan flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold">{i + 1}</span>
              <p class="text-white m-0">{q}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8">Ask What Happens After Launch</h2>
        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          This is where a lot of local web design relationships quietly fall apart. A website isn't a one-time purchase — it needs security updates, occasional content changes, and someone who understands why traffic dropped if it ever does.
        </p>
        <p class="text-white mb-4 leading-relaxed">Questions worth asking upfront:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-white mb-12 leading-relaxed">
          <li>Who do I contact if the site goes down?</li>
          <li>Is basic SEO included, or is that a separate service?</li>
          <li>Can I make small text/image changes myself, or do I need to pay for every edit?</li>
          <li>What happens if I want to switch designers later — do I own my domain, hosting, and code outright?</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8">What a Professional Website Should Deliver in 2026</h2>
        <ul class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 list-none p-0 mb-16">
          <li class="bg-brand-dark/50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-white/5 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="text-brand-accent">✦</span> <span class="text-white">Lightning-fast loading speeds</span>
          </li>
          <li class="bg-brand-dark/50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-white/5 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="text-brand-accent">✦</span> <span class="text-white">Mobile-first design</span>
          </li>
          <li class="bg-brand-dark/50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-white/5 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="text-brand-accent">✦</span> <span class="text-white">Built-in lead capture tools</span>
          </li>
          <li class="bg-brand-dark/50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-white/5 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="text-brand-accent">✦</span> <span class="text-white">Strong local SEO foundation</span>
          </li>
          <li class="bg-brand-dark/50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-white/5 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="text-brand-accent">✦</span> <span class="text-white">Modern, trustworthy branding</span>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8">Anatomy of a Page That Turns Visitors Into Leads</h2>
        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          Whether you hire us or hire somebody else, every page on the finished site needs three things. If a portfolio you're looking at doesn't have all three, ask about it.
        </p>

        <ul class="space-y-6 list-none p-0 mb-16">
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <div class="shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-cyan/10 border border-brand-cyan/20 flex items-center justify-center text-brand-cyan font-bold text-sm">1</div>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">The Hero Hook</strong>
              <span class="text-white/90">A clear value proposition that answers "What do you do?" in three seconds.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <div class="shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-cyan/10 border border-brand-cyan/20 flex items-center justify-center text-brand-cyan font-bold text-sm">2</div>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Social Proof</strong>
              <span class="text-white/90">Actual reviews from <a href="/web-design-shelby-nc/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">Shelby</a> locals to build instant credibility.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <div class="shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-cyan/10 border border-brand-cyan/20 flex items-center justify-center text-brand-cyan font-bold text-sm">3</div>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Frictionless CTA</strong>
              <span class="text-white/90">A prominent, easy-to-use button to book or call immediately.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <div class="bg-brand-dark border border-white/5 p-8 rounded-3xl mb-16">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Local SEO From Day One</h3>
          <p class="text-white/90 mb-0">
            Roughly 46% of all Google searches have local intent, and the top three map results take about 70% of the clicks in that pack. A site is built with local schema and location pages from the start ranks into that pack faster than one patched together later. If you want the full picture of what that involves, read our <a href="/blog/local-seo-essentials-2026/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">local SEO essentials guide</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8">Watch for These Red Flags</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-4 text-white mb-12 leading-relaxed">
          <li><span class="font-semibold text-white">Vague answers about SEO.</span> "We'll get you on page one of Google" with no explanation of how is a marketing line, not a strategy.</li>
          <li><span class="font-semibold text-white">No mention of mobile-first design.</span> More than half of local searches happen on a phone. If mobile isn't the first thing they talk about, that's a gap.</li>
          <li><span class="font-semibold text-white">Website builders disguised as custom work.</span> There's nothing wrong with platforms like Squarespace or Wix for some businesses, but if you're being sold "custom development" and it's actually a templated builder underneath, you should know that going in.</li>
          <li><span class="font-semibold text-white">No local presence to verify.</span> If you can't find a real local address, a real local phone number, or any trace of them in your community, that's worth a second look.</li>
          <li><span class="font-semibold text-white">Big retainers for local work.</span> If the price tag looks like a national agency for a small local business, ask what you are actually paying for.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8">What "Best" Should Actually Mean for Your Business</h2>
        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          The best web designer for a solar installer isn't necessarily the best fit for a roofing company or a family-owned restaurant — different industries need different things from a site: lead capture forms, before/after galleries, booking systems, ROI calculators, whatever actually drives that specific kind of customer to pick up the phone.
        </p>
        <p class="text-white mb-12 leading-relaxed">
          Instead of asking "who's the best web designer near me" in the abstract, it's worth asking: who's the best web designer near me for a business like mine? That's a much more answerable question, and it's the one that actually predicts whether you'll be happy with the result six months from now.
        </p>

        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          Looking for a web designer who actually understands the <a href="/web-design-shelby-nc/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">Shelby</a>, <a href="/web-design-gastonia-nc/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">Gastonia</a>, and greater western North Carolina market? <a href="/promotions/free-seo-audit/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">Get a free SEO audit</a> or <a href="/contact/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">reach out</a> and we'll tell you honestly whether we're the right fit for your business — not just tell you we're "the best."
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8">What It Costs, and How Long It Takes</h2>
        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          If cost is part of your decision, our <a href="/blog/website-cost-shelby-nc-2026/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">website cost guide for the Shelby area</a> breaks down the real price ranges, what drives them, and the questions worth asking before you hire anyone. A realistic small-business site typically takes 3–6 weeks from kickoff to launch.
        </p>

        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          — Dave Richardson<br />
          Founder / Lead Developer<br />
          Shelby Web Company<br />
          Shelby, North Carolina
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
